  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Epilepsy Pathway Innovation in Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Epilepsy Pathway Innovation in Africa (EPInA) intervenes at four key points in the pathway from incidence to management of epilepsy over the entire life course and across segments of society. It proposes to reduce the burden of epilepsy by testing interventions in the following points: i) prevention; ii) diagnosis; iii) care; and iv) socio-economic burden. These studies are conducted in four sites across Africa: Accra, Zimbabwe, Ghana; Kilifi, Kenya; Mahenge, Tanzania; and the informal settlements of Nairobi, Kenya.</narrative>
  </description>
